name: bashbug
description: |-
  GNU bashbug, version 5.2.21-release

  Bashbug is used to send mail to the Bash maintainers for when Bash doesn't behave like you'd like, or expect.

  Bashbug will start up your editor (as defined by the shell's EDITOR environment variable) with a preformatted bug report template for you to fill in. The report will be mailed to the bug-bash mailing list by default. See the manual for details.

  If you invoke bashbug by accident, just quit your editor without saving any changes to the template, and no bug report will be sent.
usage:
- 'Usage: /usr/bin/bashbug [--help] [--version] [bug-report-email-address]'
positionals:
- name: bug-report-email-address
  provenance:
    sources:
    - help-text
flags:
- spellings:
  - --help
  provenance:
    sources:
    - help-text-synopsis
- spellings:
  - --version
  provenance:
    sources:
    - help-text-synopsis
provenance:
  sources:
  - help-text
  confidence: 0.5
children_filled: true
